# UI standards

**UX governance:** [`docs/ux/UX_CONSTITUTION.md`](../../docs/ux/UX_CONSTITUTION.md), [`docs/ux/DESIGN_TOKENS.md`](../../docs/ux/DESIGN_TOKENS.md) — agent rule [`ux-standards.mdc`](./ux-standards.mdc).

## Shared components

```typescript
import { Button, Card, Spinner } from 'shared/components';
```

Do not import from `@/components/ui/*` or deep `shared/src/...` paths unless the repo already standardizes an exception.

**Button:** variants `primary` | `secondary` | `ghost` only; sizes `sm` | `md` | `lg`.

**Card:** simple wrapper — **no** `CardHeader` / `CardTitle` / `CardContent` subcomponents.

Other building blocks: `Alert`, `Badge`, `Spinner`, `Tabs`, `Switch`, `Modal`, `Input`, `Textarea` — see `shared/src/components/`.

## Text contrast (readability)

On **light** backgrounds (white, gray-50/100): use **`text-gray-700` or darker** for primary copy; **`text-gray-600` minimum** for secondary. Avoid `text-gray-500` / `400` / `300` on light surfaces.

On **dark** backgrounds: `text-gray-300`+ or `text-white` as appropriate.

Inactive UI should stay readable — prefer **`text-gray-600` minimum**, not `text-gray-500`, on light backgrounds.

